    failureMode: Object.freeze({ title: "Isolation", pattern: "internal consistency does not require anyone else's participation, which makes it easy to stop engaging with people who think differently, since their disagreement changes nothing about what you already believe.", whereItShowsUp: "conversations that could have sharpened or tested your view get quietly avoided, not from certainty that you are right, but because the friction of the conversation feels unnecessary when your position is not actually at stake.", cost: "a worldview that never gets pressure-tested by real disagreement can harden into something closer to habit than conviction, without you noticing the difference.", lever: "deliberately seek out one person a year who holds your opposite position and can argue it well, and actually let the conversation risk changing something." }),
